% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% expect-output: 50.0
% expect-output: 50.0
% expect-output: 50.0
% expect-output: 50.0
% expect-output: /nocurrentpoint
% Scenario: control points widen the box. The box of a curve encloses
% its control points, not only its ends (PLRM3 §8.2 pathbbox); a moveto
% ending the path is left out, unless it is the whole path; an empty
% path has no box. Each box is printed as llx lly urx ury, one per line.
/report { pathbbox 4 -1 roll = 3 -1 roll = exch = = } def
0 0 moveto 0 100 100 100 100 0 curveto report
50 50 moveto report
newpath 50 50 moveto report
newpath { pathbbox } stopped pop $error /errorname get ==
